# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate declares a reference mode occupation; an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gate rotates the single-particle basis. Placed back to back, the two gates prepare a *Slater determinant*; the modes start in the reference determinant and are then rotated into the target orbitals. The [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate captures that composition, and because it carries the reference occupation, transpiling it can use the rectangular [`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater \"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\"), which realizes only the *occupied* orbitals, instead of the full square decomposition an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") alone requires. That is a strictly cheaper synthesis (see the payoff at the end of this guide).\n"
msgstr "Une porte [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") déclare une occupation de modes de référence ; une porte [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") fait tourner la base à une particule. Placées l'une derrière l'autre, les deux portes préparent un *déterminant de Slater* ; les modes partent du déterminant de référence puis sont tournés vers les orbitales cibles. La porte [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") capture cette composition et, comme elle porte l'occupation de référence, sa transpilation peut utiliser la [`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater \"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\") rectangulaire, qui ne réalise que les orbitales *occupées*, au lieu de la décomposition carrée complète qu'exige une [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") seule. C'est une synthèse strictement moins coûteuse (voir le gain à la fin de ce guide).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") transpiler pass detects the [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\")-then-[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") pattern in a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") and rewrites it into [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gates, so a later synthesis stage picks up the reduced decomposition automatically. Under simulation, the rewrite is a no-op on the state: [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") is *validate-then-rotate* (it validates the reference occupation and then applies the rotation, just as the two separate gates do), so the merge unlocks the cheaper synthesis without changing the prepared state.\n"
msgstr "La passe de transpiler [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") détecte le motif [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") puis [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") dans un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") et le réécrit en portes [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), de sorte qu'une étape de synthèse ultérieure reprend automatiquement la décomposition réduite. En simulation, la réécriture n'a aucun effet sur l'état : [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") est *valider puis tourner* (elle valide l'occupation de référence puis applique la rotation, exactement comme les deux portes séparées), si bien que la fusion débloque la synthèse moins coûteuse sans modifier l'état préparé.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Throughout this guide, each circuit is drawn before and after the pass, side by side: the input on the left, and the result of running the pass on it on the right. Two helpers do that. `merge` runs the pass on a copy of the circuit (through its [`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) and converts the result back to a drawable [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\"), and `draw_merge` draws both halves into a single before/after figure:\n"
msgstr "Tout au long de ce guide, chaque circuit est dessiné avant et après la passe, côte à côte : l'entrée à gauche, et le résultat de la passe appliquée à celle-ci à droite. Deux fonctions auxiliaires s'en chargent. `merge` exécute la passe sur une copie du circuit (via son [`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) et reconvertit le résultat en un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") dessinable, et `draw_merge` dessine les deux moitiés dans une seule figure avant/après :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What gets merged {#what-gets-merged}"
msgstr "Ce qui est fusionné {#what-gets-merged}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pass recognizes three patterns, all keyed off the block-spin mode convention that [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") use. For a system with `norb` spatial orbitals, the modes `0..norb` are the spin-alpha sector, and `norb..2*norb` are the spin-beta sector. Slater determinant preparation is done per spin sector because each sector has its own (electrons, orbitals) shape.\n"
msgstr "La passe reconnaît trois motifs, tous basés sur la convention de modes par blocs de spin qu'utilisent [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") et [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\"). Pour un système à `norb` orbitales spatiales, les modes `0..norb` forment le secteur de spin alpha, et `norb..2*norb` le secteur de spin bêta. La préparation d'un déterminant de Slater se fait par secteur de spin, car chaque secteur a sa propre forme (électrons, orbitales).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full-register (or spinless) {#full-register-or-spinless}"
msgstr "Registre complet (ou sans spin) {#full-register-or-spinless}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest pattern is using [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), immediately followed by an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") on the *same* modes. This is the spinless case (one determinant over all modes) and also a spinful circuit whose rotation spans both sectors at once. The two gates fuse into a single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"
msgstr "Le motif le plus simple consiste à utiliser [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), immédiatement suivi d'une [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") sur les *mêmes* modes. C'est le cas sans spin (un déterminant sur tous les modes), mais aussi celui d'un circuit avec spin dont la rotation couvre les deux secteurs à la fois. Les deux portes fusionnent en une seule [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") :\n"

